@house_menu

- @house_simple_majority
- @house_super_majority
- @house_rep_lib_majority
- @house_defeat
- @house_lib_kingmaker
- @house_tie

@house_simple_majority
title: **Democrats** gain a majority in the House
subtitle: **Democrats**: [+ rep_r +] seats
view-if: house_majority = 1
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

The **Democrats** have secured a majority in the House of Representatives.

@house_super_majority
title: **Democrats** secure a supermajority
subtitle: **Democrats**: [+ rep_r +] seats
view-if: house_majority = 3
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

With two-thirds of the House, **Democrats** now wield veto-proof power.

@house_rep_lib_majority
title: **Democrats** and **Democratic Socialists** hold a working majority
subtitle: **Democratss**: [+ rep_r +] seats, **Democratic Socialists**: [+ dsa_r +] seats
view-if: house_majority = 0 and dem_dsa_working_majority = 1 and dsa_split = 1
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

Neither party holds an outright majority, but **Democrats**</span> and <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> together command enough seats to pass legislation if they can find common ground. Their cooperation will not come without a price.

@house_defeat
title: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> lose the House
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span>: [+ rep_r +] seats
view-if: house_majority = 0 and dem_dsa_working_majority = 0 and rep_r > rep_r
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

The <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span> have taken control of the House of Representatives.

@house_lib_kingmaker
title: <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> hold the balance of power
subtitle: <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span>: [+ lib_r +] seats
view-if: house_majority = 0 and dem_dsa_working_majority = 0 and rep_r <= dem_r and dsa_split = 1
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

No party commands a majority. The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> find themselves in the position of kingmakers — their votes will determine whether Reconstruction legislation advances or stalls.

@house_tie
title: The House is tied!
subtitle: Both parties are neck and neck
view-if: rep_r = dem_r and house_majority = 0 and dem_dsa_working_majority = 0
on-arrival: speaker_election_needed = 1

A tied House will cause major legislative deadlock in the months ahead.
